For educational purposes, you can demonstrate the process step-by-step to show how each set is merged into the result incrementally.
```python
>>> result = set()
>>> new_set = {1, 2}
>>> result |= new_set  # Equivalent to result = result.union(new_set)
>>> new_set = {3, 4}
>>> result |= new_set
>>> result
{1, 2, 3, 4}
```
